# Image scan findings OmniSync accepts for now, each with a reason and an
# expiry date (exp:); an expired entry fails the scan again.

# google.golang.org/grpc compiled into rclone 1.75.1 (usr/local/bin/rclone),
# the latest rclone release (2026-09-04). OmniSync cannot rebuild rclone with
# a fixed grpc: bump RCLONE_VERSION in the Dockerfile as soon as a release
# includes grpc 1.82.2 / 1.83.2 or newer.
#
# Status 2026-10-05: still no fixed release. rclone's master moved to the
# patched grpc on 2026-09-09 (commit ef6968730f, "to fix CVE-2026-84445"),
# but v1.75.1 is still the latest release and the v1.75-stable branch has not
# taken the fix, so it arrives with the next release (v1.76).
# Not exploitable here (GHSA-2v4p-qf9q-27wj): the panic is in the routing
# interceptor of gRPC *servers* built with xds.NewGRPCServer. rclone imports
# grpc only indirectly, through the cloud SDKs' clients, and never runs a gRPC
# server; OmniSync runs rclone only as a one-shot command (no rcd or serve),
# so nothing in the image listens for gRPC. Expiry moved from 2026-11-15 to
# 2027-01-15 to cover the next rclone release; check again then.
CVE-2026-84445 exp:2027-01-15
